      "explanation": "<p>The coordination compound [Co(ox)<sub>2</sub>(Br)(NH<sub>3</sub>)]<sup>2<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup>\nof general\nformula [M(A - A)<sub>2</sub>BC]\ncan show both geometrical and optical\nisomerism (stereoisomerism).</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45s7k5s/45bd7874-47ea-4ab5-a1ac-c24ebe62ca98/b8930d00-e744-11ec-b516-e9d14aa8a160/file-1l45s7k5t.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l45s7k5s/45bd7874-47ea-4ab5-a1ac-c24ebe62ca98/b8930d00-e744-11ec-b516-e9d14aa8a160/file-1l45s7k5t.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 239 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l45s7k5s/45bd7874-47ea-4ab5-a1ac-c24ebe62ca98/b8930d00-e744-11ec-b516-e9d14aa8a160/file-1l45s7k5t.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l45s7k5s/45bd7874-47ea-4ab5-a1ac-c24ebe62ca98/b8930d00-e744-11ec-b516-e9d14aa8a160/file-1l45s7k5t.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45s7k5s/45bd7874-47ea-4ab5-a1ac-c24ebe62ca98/b8930d00-e744-11ec-b516-e9d14aa8a160/file-1l45s7k5t.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l45s7k5s/45bd7874-47ea-4ab5-a1ac-c24ebe62ca98/b8930d00-e744-11ec-b516-e9d14aa8a160/file-1l45s7k5t.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l45s7k5s/45bd7874-47ea-4ab5-a1ac-c24ebe62ca98/b8930d00-e744-11ec-b516-e9d14aa8a160/file-1l45s7k5t.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l45s7k5s/45bd7874-47ea-4ab5-a1ac-c24ebe62ca98/b8930d00-e744-11ec-b516-e9d14aa8a160/file-1l45s7k5t.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The cis-form produces non-superimposable mirror images, i.e.\nenantiomeric pairs (optically active)</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45s939x/6801b086-8c57-4b6c-bebc-2231ab32359a/e3261940-e744-11ec-95c6-e9b0f973067d/file-1l45s939y.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l45s939x/6801b086-8c57-4b6c-bebc-2231ab32359a/e3261940-e744-11ec-95c6-e9b0f973067d/file-1l45s939y.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 239 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l45s939x/6801b086-8c57-4b6c-bebc-2231ab32359a/e3261940-e744-11ec-95c6-e9b0f973067d/file-1l45s939y.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l45s939x/6801b086-8c57-4b6c-bebc-2231ab32359a/e3261940-e744-11ec-95c6-e9b0f973067d/file-1l45s939y.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l45s939x/6801b086-8c57-4b6c-bebc-2231ab32359a/e3261940-e744-11ec-95c6-e9b0f973067d/file-1l45s939y.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l45s939x/6801b086-8c57-4b6c-bebc-2231ab32359a/e3261940-e744-11ec-95c6-e9b0f973067d/file-1l45s939y.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l45s939x/6801b086-8c57-4b6c-bebc-2231ab32359a/e3261940-e744-11ec-95c6-e9b0f973067d/file-1l45s939y.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l45s939x/6801b086-8c57-4b6c-bebc-2231ab32359a/e3261940-e744-11ec-95c6-e9b0f973067d/file-1l45s939y.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The trans-form is optically inactive.\n<br><br>So, total number of stereoisomers possible\n= cis( <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.507ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -666 778 666\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"B1\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-B1\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ) + trans = 3\n</p>"
